 "result": "My body is maze.py: it reads all of stdin as bytes, pads the grid with a wall border in a flat bytearray, finds S and E with find(), and runs a level-by-level BFS over the flat index with +-1 and +-width offsets. It prints the distance, or -1 if E is unreachable or S/E is missing. It matches all three public samples (2008, -1, 78) on repeated runs. Assay registered a baseline of 3.56528 with 6.0% noise. A variant with early exit and local append binding scored 3.385 against the incumbent's 3.368, which is within noise, so I kept the incumbent and stopped.",
